  "title": "UK Constitutional Order and Self-Determination",
  "question": "What has actually moved in the Scottish, Welsh and Irish self-determination coordination, and how are the United Kingdom, London and the City of London legally and institutionally related?",
  "bluf": "No independence was announced on September 13. A reported SNP-Plaid Cymru-Sinn Fein memorandum scheduled for September 14 is a political-coordination object, not a transfer of referendum power or constitutional change. The governed graph now contains 211 nodes and 308 typed relations across seven lenses. Its DLT and Documents & rulebooks layers show that the transition occurs through a hierarchy of Acts and statutory instruments, regulator rules and firm-specific approvals, public operating terms, private infrastructure rulebooks, claim/custody/customer contracts, and correction or failure documents. The entities remain recognizable while the documents between them determine whether a ledger entry has legal effect.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-13T17:59:00-04:00",
  "use_note": "The September 13 orientation precedes the reported meeting. Replace no claim with the unsigned instrument; preserve political, office, statutory, consent, implementation and operative clocks separately.",
